  "body": "### Summary\nTwo minor limits of the shared PR-reference parser (`tooling/common/pr_refs.py`, #1198 / PR #1289) were left after the review cap was reached. Neither affects any of the 567 PR bodies on ezzz/HFRnow today.\n\n### Scope\n1. A ref that follows `.` mid-line still opens a sentence. `Not done. Closes #12 (later).` and `We tried it. Fixes #12, partly.` both give closing `[12]`. The rule is kept on purpose so that #303, #259 and #257 still read. Pin it with a table case in `scripts/tests/test_pr_refs.py` and state the limit in the module docstring.\n2. `Refs LOT-118, Refs #209:` (as in #638) no longer yields #209, because `Refs LOT-\\d+` does not count as a preceding reference. A PR written this way would not get its issue marked claimed by the sweep. Fix: let a `Refs LOT-\\d+` count as a preceding ref, with a table case.\n\n### Blocked by\n#1289\n\n### Sources\nAdversarial review round 3 of PR #1289 (Opus 5.5, r1289, head 2ef82b5c), findings 1 and 2.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Both cases are in `test_pr_refs_agree`. Case 2 is shown red before the fix.\n- [ ] The old-vs-new comparison over the merged bodies is re-run, and the delta is stated on the PR.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
